import SwiftUI
import KwipMLCore

enum GameEpisodeLessonContent {
    static let objective="This canvas connects an authored take-away game to a small numeric model. **Authored game** defines a pile of 21 objects. Players remove one, two or three objects; taking the last object wins. **Game observations** receives the remaining fraction as one float32 number. **Action logits** produces three scores, one for each candidate move. **Policy scores** exposes that architecture to the session. **Bounded game session** initializes it once and plays against a random legal opponent.\n\nThis is inference, not learning: the randomly initialized policy does not improve. The two View blocks inspect complete episode outcomes and applied moves."
    static let terms="- **Observation:** the ordered numeric information the game exposes to a player.\n- **Logit:** an unconstrained score for one fixed candidate action.\n- **Legal mask:** the current allowed actions; indices never shift as moves become illegal.\n- **Entrant A/B:** a policy, distinct from player seats 0/1.\n- **Truncation:** an episode stopped by a limit, with no invented draw or terminal outcome."
    static let steps=[
        "Select [Authored game](kwip-node://data/rules) and inspect its rules and tests. The remaining observation is state.remaining / 21. Action candidates are take: 1, take: 2 and take: 3 in that order. Validate the authored tests before changing rules. Close the editor when ready.",
        "Follow [Game observations](kwip-node://model/observation) through [Action logits](kwip-node://model/policy-head) to [Policy scores](kwip-node://model/output). One input value becomes three scores. The model does not remove objects itself; the session interprets its highest legal score as an action. A score for taking three is masked out when fewer than three remain.",
        "Select [Bounded game session](kwip-node://control/session) → Configure game session. Players uses a Canvas definition for A and Random legal for B. Read the initialization seed, named input and Greedy selection. Observations & actions explains exact [1, N] input and [1, A] output requirements. Validate bindings probes the actual model without playing episodes or running downstream writes. Close or Apply after validation.",
        "Run Flow. Select [Inspect episodes](kwip-node://data/episodes) to read each seat assignment, status, winner and move count. Alternating seats uses an even episode count so each entrant occupies both seats. Compare terminal results separately from truncated or failed attempts; a short random match is not a learning-quality claim.",
        "Open [Inspect moves](kwip-node://data/moves). Double-click before, action or after to inspect full JSON in the shared paged cell viewer. A move identifies the player, entrant and fixed action index. Enable decision capture for a small rerun if you want observations, legal masks, logits and sampling probabilities; capture affects storage, not the policy's behavior.",
        "Try a one-move limit in Configure game session → Run limits. Validate, Apply and run again: the episode should say moveLimit, with no winner or draw credit. Restore a useful limit, then Save. To compare rules with a different observation/action width, explicitly update the model as well; the runner refuses mismatches instead of reshaping or substituting random play."
    ]
    static let boundary="This editable practice is unscored. Two-player deterministic rules, finite actions and one numeric float32 policy input/output. Canvas parameters initialize once; same-snapshot policies share immutable weights. Saved canvas checkpoints require verified completed History. Use Learn from bounded self-play for search, paired policy/value learning and resume. Imported language/classifier adapters, arbitrary rule scripts and a visual lab remain separate work. Full outputs share the existing 8 MB cap; limits never become draws."
}
struct GameEpisodeLearningView:View {
    @ObservedObject var store:WorkspaceStore
    var body:some View {Button("Open bounded game episodes practice"){_=store.loadComponentWorkflowExample(GameEpisodePractice.lessonID,device:"cpu")}.buttonStyle(FlatButtonStyle()).disabled(store.isBusy)}
}
